=== meta ===
bypass: 117
rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: a skip mark bound to a name and applied by it still blocks
origin: #260 M1: the binding is no longer a module-level skip call, so the decorator that names it
origin2: is read as the mark it holds (pytest.mark.skip), on the test it skips.
=== before: tests/test_calc.py ===
import sys

import pytest


def test_add():
    assert 1 + 1 == 2
=== after: tests/test_calc.py ===
import sys

import pytest

skip_slow = pytest.mark.skip(reason="slow")


@skip_slow
def test_add():
    assert 1 + 1 == 2
